          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            An object in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
            is fibrant if all morphisms into it have extensions along acyclic cofibrations. An
            %strong algebraic fibrant object
            is a fibrant object equipped with a
            %em choice
            of such extensions.
          %p
            Under mild conditions, the category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Alg
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Alg C
            of algebraic fibrant objects in a model category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            forms itself naturally a model category which is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalence"} Quillen equivalent
            to
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Alg
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Alg C
            is always a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+fibrant+objects"} category of fibrant objects
          %h2#definition Definition
          .un_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrantly+generated+model+category"} cofibrantly generated model category
              such that
            %ul
              %li
                all acyclic cofibrations are
                = succeed "s." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monomorphism"} monomorphism
            %p
              Choose a set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi j
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi B
                      %mi j
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi j
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi J
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{A_j \to B_j\}_{j \in J}
              of acyclic cofibrations such that
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  the
                  = succeed "s" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/domain"} domain
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi A
                          %mi j
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_j
                  are
                  = succeed "s;" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+object"} small object
              %li
                %p
                  an object
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in C
                  is fibrant precisely if it has the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+lifting+property"} right lifting property
                  against these morphisms.
            %p
              An
              %strong algebraic fibrant object
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              is a fibrant object of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              together with a choice of lifts (“fillers”)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi σ
                      %mi j
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi B
                      %mi j
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma_j : B_j \to X
              in
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi A
                              %mi j
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo ↗
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi σ
                                    %mi j
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi B
                              %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    A_j &amp;\to&amp; X
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp; \nearrow_{\mathrlap{\sigma_j}}
                    \\\
                    B_j
                    }
            %p
              for each morphism
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi A
                        %mi j
                      %mo →
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_j \to X
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi j
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi J
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j \in J
            %p
              Write
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Alg
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Alg C
              for the category whose objects are algebraic fibrant objects in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              and whose morphisms are morphisms in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              that respect the chosen lifts.
          .un_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              The set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi J
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
              can be taken to be that of all generating acyclic cofibrations, if their domains are small. But often there are smaller subsets that still characterize all fibrant objects.
          #ModelStructureTheorem.un_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/forgetful+functor"} forgetful functor
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction"} adjunction
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi F
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mi Alg
                    %mi C
                    %mover
                      %munder
                        %mo →
                        %mi U
                      %mover
                        %mo ←
                        %mi F
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (F \dashv U) : Alg C \stackrel{\overset{F}{\leftarrow}}{\underset{U}{\to}} C
            %p
              induces the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transferred+model+structure"} transferred model structure
              on
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Alg
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Alg C
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Alg
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Alg C
              are those of the underlying morphisms in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %p
              In particular, every object in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Alg
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Alg C
              is fibrant.
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+adjunction"} Quillen adjunction
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi F
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (F \dashv U)
              is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalence"} Quillen equivalence
          %p
            This is (
            %a{:href => "#Nikolaus"}> Nikolaus, theorem 2.20
            )
          .un_remark
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %p
              Since fibrations in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Alg
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Alg C
              are created in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Alg
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Alg C
              is fibrant. Thus almost any model category is equivalent to one in which all objects are fibrant. However, in general not all objects in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Alg
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Alg C
              will be cofibrant, even if this was true in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              itself.
          %h2#details Details
          %p
            We spell out the constructions and lemmas that yield the
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#ModelStructureTheorem"} theorem on the model structure
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Alg
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Alg C
          %h3#the_left_adjoint The left adjoint
          %p
            We describe explicitly the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo :
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mi Alg
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F : C \to Alg C
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/forgetful+functor"} forgetful functor
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo :
                    %mi Alg
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U : Alg C \to C
            = succeed "\u2018s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Richard+Garner"} Richard Garner
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+object+argument"} small object argument
            (
            %a{:href => "#Garner"}> Garner
            ).
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in C
            define a new object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_\infty
            inductively as follows.
          .un_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_1
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushout"} pushout
              (in
              = succeed ")" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                            %msub
                              %mi A
                              %mi j
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                            %msub
                              %mi B
                              %mi j
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi X
                              %mn 1
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\coprod A_j &amp;\to&amp; X
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    \\coprod B_j &amp;\to&amp; X_1
                    }
                    \\,,
            %p
              here the disjoint unition is taken over all
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j
              and all morphisms
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi A
                        %mi j
                      %mo →
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_j \to X
          .un_defn
            %h6#remark_3 Remark
            %p
              This pushout adds all possible “
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/horn"}> horn
              ” fillers to
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi B
                        %mi j
                      %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B_j \to X_1
            %p
              Since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi j
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                    %msub
                      %mi B
                      %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \coprod A_j \to \coprod B_j
              is an acyclic cofibration in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to X_1
              is a monomorphism. This implies that if an
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi j
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_j \to X_1
              factors through
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to X_1
              then it does so uniquely.
          #DefOfXInfty.un_defn
            %h6#definition_4 Definition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_2
              be the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushout"} pushout
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                            %msub
                              %mi A
                              %mi j
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi X
                              %mn 1
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                            %msub
                              %mi B
                              %mi j
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi X
                              %mn 2
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\coprod A_j &amp;\to&amp; X_1
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    \\coprod B_j &amp;\to&amp; X_2
                    }
                    \\,,
            %p
              where now the coproduct is over those morphisms
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi j
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_j \to X
              that do
              %em not
              factor throuth
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to X_1
            %p Proceeding this way yields a sequence of acyclic cofibrations
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 2
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 3
                    %mo →
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    X \to X_1 \to X_2 \to X_3 \to \cdots
                    \\,.
            %p We set
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo :
                    %mo =
                    %munder
                      %mi lim
                      %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 2
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 3
                    %mo →
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    X_\infty :=  \lim_\to (X \to X_1 \to X_2 \to X_3 \to \cdots )
            %p
              be the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimit
              over this sequence.
          .un_observation
            %h6#observation Observation
            %p
              The object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_\infty
              inherits canonical fillers: since by all
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_j
              are
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+object"} small object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi j
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_j \to X_\infty
              factors through one of the intermediate
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_i
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi j
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi B
                      %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_j \to B_j
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi J
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
              the corresponding morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi B
                      %mi j
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B_j \to X_{i+1} \to X_\infty
              provides a filler.
          .un_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              The assignment
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F : X \to X_\infty
              with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_\infty
              regarded as an algebraic fibrant objects as above constitutes a left
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functor"} adjoint functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo :
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mi Alg
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F : C \to Alg C
              to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/forgetful+functor"} forgetful functor
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mo :
                      %mi Alg
                      %mi C
                      %mo →
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U : Alg C \to C
            %p
              The unit of this
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction"} adjunction
              is the inclusion
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to X_\infty
              given by the above construction and is hence a weak equivalence.
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              We establish the hom-isomorphism of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction"} adjunction
              and its construction by the unit of the adjunction: For any
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Z
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Alg
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Z \in Alg C
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi : X \to U(Z)
              any morphism in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+diagram"} commuting diagram
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi ϕ
                          %mtd
                            %mi Z
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo ↗
                              %mrow
                                %mo ∃
                                %mo !
                                %msub
                                  %mi ϕ
                                  %mn ∞
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi X
                              %mn ∞
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    X &amp;\stackrel{\phi}{\to}&amp; Z
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp; \nearrow_{\exists ! \phi_\infty}
                    \\\
                    X_\infty
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              Since by assumption
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Z
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Z
              has all fillers we have commuting diagrams
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi A
                              %mi j
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi ϕ
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi B
                              %mi j
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi Z
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    A_j &amp;\to&amp; X
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{\phi}}
                    \\\
                    B_j &amp;\to&amp; Z
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p By the universality of the pushout these induce unique morphisms
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi ϕ
                          %mtd
                            %mi Z
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo ↗
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi ϕ
                                  %mn 1
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi X
                              %mn 1
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    X &amp;\stackrel{\phi}{\to}&amp; Z
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp; \nearrow_{\phi_1 }
                    \\\
                    X_1
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              By induction this induces morphisms
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mi n
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi n
                    %mo →
                    %mi Z
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi_n : X_n \to Z
              that form a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocone"} cocone
              under
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mn 1
                      %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mn 2
                      %mo →
                      %mi ⋯
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X \to X_1 \to X_2 \to \cdots )
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi_\infty
              as indicated.
          .un_corollary
            %h6#corollary Corollary
            %p
              The morphisms
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mi F
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi j
                    %mo →
                    %mi F
                    %msub
                      %mi B
                      %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F(j) : F A_j \to F B_j
              have
              = succeed "s." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/retract"} retract
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p
              Since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
              to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              the condition that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi j
                    %mo →
                    %mi F
                    %msub
                      %mi B
                      %mi j
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi r
                    %mi F
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F A_j \to F B_j \stackrel{r}{\to} F A_j
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity"} identity
              is equivalent to its
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunct"} adjunct
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi A
                              %mi j
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi j
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi B
                              %mi j
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi r
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi A
                              %mi j
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo ↘
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mover
                                  %mi r
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi U
                            %mi F
                            %msub
                              %mi A
                              %mi j
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %mi U
                                %mi F
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi j
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mi U
                            %mi F
                            %msub
                              %mi B
                              %mi j
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %mi U
                                %mi F
                                %mi r
                          %mtd
                            %mi U
                            %mi F
                            %msub
                              %mi A
                              %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    A_j &amp;\stackrel{j}{\to}&amp; B_j &amp;\stackrel{r}{\to}&amp; A_j
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow &amp;\searrow^{\mathrlap{\tilde r}}&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    U F A_j &amp;\stackrel{U F (j)}{\to}&amp; U F B_j &amp;\stackrel{U F r}{\to} &amp; U F A_j
                    }
            %p
              being the unit of the adjunction
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi A
                        %mi j
                      %mo →
                      %mi U
                      %mi F
                      %msub
                        %mi A
                        %mi j
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_j \to U F A_j
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi r
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde r
              to be the (unique) filler for this morphism.
          %h3#Monadicity Monadicity of the forgetful functor
          %p
            We now give a formal justification for calling the objects of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Alg
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Alg C
            %em algebraic
            objects by showing that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Alg
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Alg C
            is the category of algebras over an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+theory"} algebraic theory
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebras+over+a+monad"} algebra over the monad
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo ∘
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \circ U
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
          .un_theorem
            %h6#theorem_2 Theorem
            %p
              The functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo :
                    %mi Alg
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U : Alg C \to C
              is
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monadic"} monadic
          %p
            This is (
            %a{:href => "#Nikolaus"}> Nikolaus, prop. 24
            )
          .proof
            %h6#proof_3 Proof
            %p
              By one of the equivalent statements of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Beck%27s+monadicity+theorem"} Beck's monadicity theorem
              we have to check that
            %ol
              %li
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
                has a
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
              %li
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
                reflects
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphisms"} isomorphisms
                (i.e. it is
                = succeed ")," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conservative+functor"} conservative
              %li
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi D
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
                has, and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/preserved+limit"} preserves
                = succeed "-split" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi U
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            %p The first item we already checked above.
            %p
              For the second item it is sufficient to observe that if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : X \to Y
              is a morphism in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Alg
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Alg C
              such that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U f
              has an inverse
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi g
                      %mo :
                      %mi U
                      %mi Y
                      %mo →
                      %mi U
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g : U Y \to U X
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
              must preserve fillers, hence itself constitutes the underlying morphism of an inverse if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Alg
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Alg C
            %p
              For the third item, let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo ,
                    %mi g
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f,g : X \to Y
              be two morphisms in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Alg
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Alg C
              such that the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coequalizer"} coequalizer
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mi X
                    %mover
                      %munder
                        %mo →
                        %mrow
                          %mi U
                          %mi g
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mrow
                          %mi U
                          %mi f
                    %mi U
                    %mi Y
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi π
                    %mi Q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    U X \stackrel{\overset{U f}{\to}}{\underset{U g}{\to}}
                    U Y
                    \\stackrel{\pi}{\to}
                    Q
            %p
              exists in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/section"} section
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi s
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi π
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi t
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(f)
              such that
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi s
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi π
                      %mo =
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi t
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi t
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s \circ \pi = U(t) \circ t
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q
              with fillers such that it becomes the coequalizer of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo ,
                    %mi g
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f,g
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Alg
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Alg C
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi h
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi j
                    %mo →
                    %mi Q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h : A_j \to Q
              a horn, declare that its filler is the the chosen filler of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi s
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi h
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s \circ h
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi A
                              %mi j
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi h
                          %mtd
                            %mi Q
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi s
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo ↘
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi Id
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi B
                              %mi j
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi π
                          %mtd
                            %mi Q
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    A_j &amp;\stackrel{h}{\to}&amp; Q
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{s}} &amp; \searrow^{\mathrlap{Id}}
                    \\\
                    B_j &amp;\to&amp; Y &amp;\stackrel{\pi}{\to} &amp; Q
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              We check now that this choice indeed makes
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q
              the coequalizer in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Alg
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Alg C
            %p
              First of all we need to check that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi π
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi
              preserves the chosen fillers.
            %p So given a filler
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi A
                              %mi j
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi k
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo ↗
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mover
                                  %mi k
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi B
                              %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    A_j &amp;\stackrel{k}{\to}&amp; Y
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp; \nearrow_{\mathrlap{\hat k}}
                    \\\
                    B_j
                    }
            %p
              it is sent by
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi π
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi
              to the filler
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi A
                              %mi j
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi k
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi π
                          %mtd
                            %mi Q
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↗
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo ↗
                              %mrow
                                %mi π
                                %mover
                                  %mi k
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi B
                              %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    A_j &amp;\stackrel{k}{\to}&amp; Y &amp;\stackrel{\pi}{\to}&amp; Q
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp; \nearrow &amp;&amp; \nearrow_{\pi \hat k}
                    \\\
                    B_j
                    }
            %p
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi π
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi k
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi A
                              %mi j
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi k
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi π
                          %mtd
                            %mi Q
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi s
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi π
                          %mtd
                            %mi Q
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo ↗
                              %mover
                                %mi r
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo ↗
                              %mrow
                                %mi π
                                %mover
                                  %mi r
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi B
                              %mi j
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    A_j &amp;\stackrel{k}{\to}&amp; Y &amp;\stackrel{\pi}{\to}&amp; Q &amp;\stackrel{s}{\to}&amp; Y &amp;\stackrel{\pi}{\to}&amp; Q
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; &amp;&amp; &amp; \nearrow_{\hat r} &amp;&amp; \nearrow_{\pi \hat r}
                    \\\
                    B_j
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              Now use the relation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi t
                    %mo =
                    %mi Id
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(f) t = Id
              to rewrite the first diagram equivalently as
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi A
                              %mi j
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi k
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi t
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %mi U
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi f
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi π
                          %mtd
                            %mi Q
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo ↗
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mover
                                  %mi g
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo ↗
                              %mrow
                                %mi π
                                %mover
                                  %mi k
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi B
                              %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    A_j &amp;\stackrel{k}{\to}&amp; Y &amp;\stackrel{t}{\to}&amp; X &amp;\stackrel{U(f)}{\to}&amp;
                    Y &amp;\stackrel{\pi}{\to}&amp; Q
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;  \nearrow_{\mathrlap{\hat g}} &amp;&amp;  \nearrow_{\pi \hat k}
                    \\\
                    B_j
                    }
            %p
              and the relation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi t
                    %mo =
                    %mi s
                    %mi π
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(g) t =  s \pi
              to rewrite the second diagram equivalently as
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi A
                              %mi j
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi k
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi t
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %mi U
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi g
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi π
                          %mtd
                            %mi Q
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo ↗
                              %mover
                                %mi r
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo ↗
                              %mrow
                                %mi π
                                %mover
                                  %mi r
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi B
                              %mi j
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    A_j &amp;\stackrel{k}{\to}&amp; Y &amp;\stackrel{t}{\to}&amp; X &amp;\stackrel{U(g)}{\to}&amp; Y &amp;\stackrel{\pi}{\to}&amp; Q
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; &amp;&amp; &amp; \nearrow_{\hat r} &amp;&amp; \nearrow_{\pi \hat r}
                    \\\
                    B_j
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              This show that the fillers
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi k
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat k
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi r
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat r
              are images under
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(f)
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi g
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(g)
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi π
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi
              coequalizes, it follows that
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi π
                      %mover
                        %mi k
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                      %mo =
                      %mi π
                      %mover
                        %mi r
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi \hat k = \pi \hat r
            %p
              Finally we need to show that the coequalizing morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi π
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Alg
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Alg C
              thus established is indeed universal with this property.
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo :
                    %mi Y
                    %mo →
                    %mi Z
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi : Y \to Z
              a coequalizing morphism in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Alc
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Alc C
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q
              is a coequalizer in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              already gives a unique morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mi Q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi_Q
              in
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %munder
                                %mo →
                                %mi g
                              %mover
                                %mo →
                                %mi f
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi π
                          %mtd
                            %mi Q
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mi ϕ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo ↙
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mo ∃
                                  %mo !
                                  %msub
                                    %mi ϕ
                                    %mi Q
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi Z
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    X &amp; \stackrel{\overset{f}{\to}}{\underset{g}{\to}} &amp; Y
                    \&amp;\stackrel{\pi}{\to} &amp; Q
                    \\\
                    \&amp;&amp; {}^{\mathllap{\phi}}\downarrow &amp; \swarrow_{\mathrlap{\exists ! \phi_Q}}
                    \\\
                    \&amp;&amp; Z
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              So it is sufficient to observe that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mi Q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi_Q
              preserves chosen fillers. But this is true be the above construction, which says that the chosen fillers in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q
              are the images of the chosen fillers in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
          %h3#Solidity Solidity of the forgetful functor
          .un_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/forgetful+functor"} forgetful functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo :
                    %mi Alg
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U : Alg C \to C
              is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/solid+functor"} solid functor
          %p We discuss the proof for a slightly simpler statement, from which the full statement follows easily.
          #SolidityLemma.un_lemma
            %h6#lemma Lemma
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              be an algebraic fibrant object,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              an object in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              and
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi Y
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    f : Y \to X
            %p
              a morphism in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              (really:
              = succeed ")." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(Y) \to X
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi X
                      %mn ∞
                      %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X^f_\infty
              and a morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %msubsup
                      %mi X
                      %mn ∞
                      %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to X^f_\infty
              such that the composite
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %msubsup
                      %mi X
                      %mn ∞
                      %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Y\to X \to X^f_{\infty}
            %p
              is a morphism of algebraic fibrant objects and it is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/initial+object"} initial
              with this property:
            %p
              for every morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Z
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi : X \to Z
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Z
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Z
              an algebraic fibrant object such that the composite
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Z
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y \to X \to Z
              preserves distinguished fillers, there exists a unique morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo :
                    %msubsup
                      %mi X
                      %mn ∞
                      %mi f
                    %mo →
                    %mi Z
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi_\infty : X^f_\infty \to Z
              such that we have a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+diagram"} commutative diagram
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mi f
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo ↘
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi alg
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi ϕ
                          %mtd
                            %mi Z
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo ↗
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mo ∃
                                  %mo !
                                  %msub
                                    %mi ϕ
                                    %mn ∞
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msubsup
                              %mi X
                              %mn ∞
                              %mi f
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    Y
                    \\\
                    {}^{\mathllap{f}}\downarrow &amp; \searrow^{\mathrlap{alg}}
                    \\\
                    X &amp;\stackrel{\phi}{\to}&amp; Z
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp; \nearrow_{\mathrlap{\exists ! \phi_\infty}}
                    \\\
                    X^f_\infty
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              Moreover, if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monomorphism"} monomorphism
              in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %msubsup
                      %mi X
                      %mn ∞
                      %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to X^f_\infty
              is an acyclic cofibration.
          %p
            This is (
            %a{:href => "#Nikolaus"}> Nikolaus, prop. 2.6
            ).
          %p
            The naive idea would be to equip
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            with distinguished fillers
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mover
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \hat k
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi A
                            %mi j
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mi k
                        %mtd
                          %mi Y
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mi f
                        %mtd
                          %mi X
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mo ↗
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mover
                                %mi k
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mo ↗
                            %mrow
                              %mi f
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mover
                                  %mi k
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi B
                            %mi j
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  A_j &amp;\stackrel{k}{\to}&amp; Y &amp;\stackrel{f}{\to}&amp; X
                  \\\
                  \\downarrow &amp; \nearrow_{\mathrlap{\hat k}} &amp;&amp; \nearrow_{f \mathrlap{\hat k}}
                  \\\
                  B_j
                  }
          %p
            for each distinguished filler
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi k
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat k
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            in many ways, this will not give a unique notion of filler. Therefore we shall iteratively form colimits that equate these potentially different fillers.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_4 Proof
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
              be the set of morphisms of the form
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi h
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi j
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h : A_j \to X
              that factor through
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo :
                      %mi Y
                      %mo →
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : Y \to X
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi h
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h \in H
              let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mi h
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_h
              be the set of images of distinuished fillers
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi B
                        %mi j
                      %mo →
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B_j \to X
            %p Set
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi H
                    %mo :
                    %mo =
                    %munder
                      %mi lim
                      %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %msub
                                %mi B
                                %mi j
                              %msub
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mi h
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %msub
                                %mi B
                                %mrow
                                  %mi j
                                  %mo ′
                              %msub
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mrow
                                  %mi h
                                  %mo ′
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mi ⋯
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mrow
                                %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                  %mrow
                                    %mi ϕ
                                    %mo ∈
                                    %msub
                                      %mi F
                                      %mi h
                              %mo ↘
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                                %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                  %mrow
                                    %mi ϕ
                                    %mo ′
                                    %mo ∈
                                    %msub
                                      %mi F
                                      %mrow
                                        %mi h
                                        %mo ′
                            %mtd
                              %mi ⋯
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mi X
                      %mo )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    X_H := \lim_\to
                    \\left(
                    \\array{
                    (B_j)_h &amp;&amp; (B_{j'})_{h'} &amp;&amp; \cdots
                    \\\
                    \&amp; {}_{\mathllap{\phi \in F_h}}\searrow &amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{\phi' \in F_{h'}}}
                    \&amp; \cdots
                    \\\
                    \&amp;&amp; X
                    }
                    \\right)
            %p
              where on the right we take the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimit
              over the diagram with one object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi B
                      %mi j
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi h
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (B_j)_h
              per morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi h
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi j
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h : A_j \to X
              that factors through
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi B
                      %mi j
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi h
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (B_j)_h \to X
              per induced distinguished filler obtained from a choice of factorization through
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            %p
              This comes with a canonica
              = succeed "-morphism" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocone"} cocone
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mi H
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to X_H
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mrow
                        %mi H
                        %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_{H'}
              by coequalizing the different ways morphisms into
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_H
              may factor through
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi H
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mrow
                        %mi H
                        %mo ′
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mrow
                        %mi H
                        %mo ″
                    %mo →
                    %mi ⋯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    X \to X_H \to X_{H'} \to X_{H''} \to \cdots
            %p and set
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi X
                      %mn 0
                      %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mo =
                    %munder
                      %mi lim
                      %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi H
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mrow
                        %mi H
                        %mo ′
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mrow
                        %mi H
                        %mo ″
                    %mo →
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    X_0^f := \lim_\to (X \to X_H \to X_{H'} \to X_{H''} \to \cdots)
                    \\,.
            %p
              Notice that if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monomorphism"} monomorphism
              then all factorizations are unique and hence
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %msubsup
                      %mi X
                      %mn 0
                      %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to X_0^f
              is an
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
            %p
              The object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi X
                      %mn 0
                      %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_0^f
              can be seen to have the desired universal factorization property. But it may not yet be itself algebraically fibrant. So we conclude by essentially applying the construction of the left adjoint
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi X
                      %mn 1
                      %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_1^f
              be the pushout
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                              %mi j
                            %msub
                              %mi A
                              %mi j
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %msubsup
                              %mi X
                              %mn 0
                              %mi f
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                              %mi j
                            %msub
                              %mi B
                              %mi j
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %msubsup
                              %mi X
                              %mn 1
                              %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\coprod_j A_j &amp;\to&amp; X_0^f
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    \\coprod_j B_j &amp;\to&amp; X_1^f
                    }
            %p
              where now the coproduct is over all morphisms that do not factor through
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              and obtain a sequence
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi X
                      %mn 0
                      %mi f
                    %mo →
                    %msubsup
                      %mi X
                      %mn 1
                      %mi f
                    %mo →
                    %msubsup
                      %mi X
                      %mn 2
                      %mi f
                    %mo →
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    X_0^f \to X_1^f \to X_2^f \to \cdots
                    \\,.
            %p Finally we set
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi X
                      %mn ∞
                      %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mo =
                    %munder
                      %mi lim
                      %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mi X
                      %mn 0
                      %mi f
                    %mo →
                    %msubsup
                      %mi X
                      %mn 1
                      %mi f
                    %mo →
                    %msubsup
                      %mi X
                      %mn 2
                      %mi f
                    %mo →
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    X_\infty^f := \lim_\to(X_0^f \to X_1^f \to X_2^f \to \cdots)
                    \\,.
            %p One checks that this has the claimed properties (…).
            %p
              As before, the inclusion
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi X
                      %mn 0
                      %mi f
                    %mo →
                    %msubsup
                      %mi X
                      %mn ∞
                      %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_0^f \to X_\infty^f
              is an acyclic cofibration. Hence by the above remarks in the case that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              is a monomorphism also
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %msubsup
                      %mi X
                      %mn ∞
                      %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to X_\infty^f
              is an acyclic cofibration.
          %p
            By replacing in this proof factorization through a single
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            by factorization through a family of
            = succeed "s" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/solid+functor"} solid functor
          %h3#LimitsAndColimits Limits and colimits of algebraic objects
          .un_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              The category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Alg
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Alg C
              has all
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limit"} limit
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimit
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %p
              The limits and the
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filtered+colimit"} filtered colimit
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/created+limit"} created
              by
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
          .proof
            %h6#proof_5 Proof
            %p
              Consider first limits: for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mo :
                    %mi J
                    %mo →
                    %mi Alg
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K : J \to Alg C
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagram"} diagram
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi lim
                      %mo ←
                    %mi U
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lim_{\leftarrow} U K
              its limit in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi j
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi lim
                      %mo ←
                    %mi U
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_j \to \lim_{\leftarrow} U K
              be a horn. Since all the composite maps
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi J
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi lim
                      %mo ←
                    %mi U
                    %mi K
                    %mo →
                    %mi U
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_J \to \lim_{\leftarrow} U K \to U K(j)
              have distinguished fillers and since the morphisms between these respect these fillers, we get a cone of fillers with tip
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi B
                      %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B_j
              over
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mi K
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U K
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi B
                      %mi j
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi lim
                      %mo ←
                    %mi U
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B_j \to \lim_{\leftarrow} U K
              provides then a distinguished filler for the limit. By the same argument, any cone
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi const
                      %mi T
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi lim
                      %mo ←
                    %mi U
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} const_T \to \lim_{\leftarrow} U K
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Alg
                      %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Alg_C
              whose underlying cone in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              is a limiting cone is also limiting in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Alg
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Alg C
            %p
              Now consider
              = succeed "s." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filtered+colimit"} filtered colimit
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_j
              are
              = succeed "s." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+object"} small object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mo :
                    %mi I
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K : I \to C
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filtered+diagram"} filtered diagram
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                    %mo :
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi lim
                      %mo →
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L := \lim_{\to} K
              its
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filtered+colimit"} filtered colimit
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi j
                    %mo →
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_j \to L
              factors through one of the
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi K
                        %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K_i
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi B
                        %mi j
                      %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mi K
                        %mi i
                      %mo →
                      %mi L
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B_j \to K_i \to L
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
              nor the filler
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi B
                      %mi j
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi K
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B_j \to K_i
              are uniquely determined, its image in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
              is. This makes
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
              an object in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Alg
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Alg C
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Alg
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Alg C
            %p
              Now for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mo :
                    %mi J
                    %mo →
                    %mi Alg
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K : J \to Alg C
              a general diagram with colimit
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo :
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi lim
                      %mo →
                    %mi U
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X := \lim_\to U K
              in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/solid+functor"} solid functor
              to deduce that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi X
                      %mn ∞
                      %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_\infty^f
              is the colimit of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Alg
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Alg C
          %p
            While this gives a general prescription for computing colimits, the following lemma asserts a slightly simpler way for computing certain
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushout"} pushout
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Alg
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Alg C
          #PushoutLemma.un_lemma
            %h6#lemma_2 Lemma
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i : A \to B
              be a morphism in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              and
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi F
                            %mi A
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mi F
                                  %mi i
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi F
                            %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    F A &amp;\to&amp; Y
                    \\\
                    {}^{\mathllap{F i}}\downarrow
                    \\\
                    F B
                    }
            %p
              a diagram in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Alg
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Alg C
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  its
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushout"} pushout
                  in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Alg
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Alg C
                  is
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi B
                          %msub
                            %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                            %mi A
                          %mi U
                          %mi Y
                          %msubsup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mn ∞
                            %mi f
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (B \coprod_A U Y)_\infty^f
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo :
                        %mi U
                        %mi Y
                        %mo →
                        %mi B
                        %msub
                          %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                          %mi A
                        %mi U
                        %mi Y
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : U Y \to B \coprod_A U Y
                  is the canonical morphism;
              %li
                %p
                  if
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo :
                        %mi A
                        %mo →
                        %mi B
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i : A \to B
                  is an acyclic cofibration then so is
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi Y
                          %mo →
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi B
                          %msub
                            %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                            %mi A
                          %mi U
                          %mi Y
                          %msubsup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mn ∞
                            %mi f
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y\to (B \coprod_A U Y)_\infty^f
          %p
            This is (
            %a{:href => "#Nikolaus"}> Nikolaus, prop 2.14
            ).
          .proof
            %h6#proof_6 Proof
            %p
              First check that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi B
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                      %mi A
                    %mi U
                    %mi Y
                    %msubsup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mn ∞
                      %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (B \coprod_A U Y)_\infty^f
              has the universal property of the pushout: for any
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Z
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Alg
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Z \in Alg C
              we have by the
              %a{:href => "#SolidityLemma"} above proposition
              that morphisms
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi B
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                      %mi A
                    %mi U
                    %mi Y
                    %msubsup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mn ∞
                      %mi f
                    %mo →
                    %mi Z
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (B \coprod_A U Y)_\infty^f \to Z
              are in bijection to morphisms
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                      %mi A
                    %mi U
                    %mi Y
                    %mo →
                    %mi U
                    %mi Z
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B \coprod_A U Y \to U Z
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              such that the composition
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mi Y
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi f
                    %mi B
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                      %mi A
                    %mi U
                    %mi Y
                    %mo →
                    %mi U
                    %mi Z
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    U Y \stackrel{f}{\to} B \coprod_A U Y \to U Z
            %p preserves distinguished fillers.
            %p
              This in turn is the same as a morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi g
                      %mn 1
                    %mo :
                    %mi Y
                    %mo →
                    %mi Z
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g_1 : Y \to Z
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Alg
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Alg C
              and a morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi g
                      %mn 2
                    %mo :
                    %mi B
                    %mo →
                    %mi U
                    %mi Z
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g_2 : B \to U Z
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              that agree on
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction"} adjunction
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi F
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (F \dashv U)
              this corresponds to an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunct"} adjunct
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mover
                          %mi g
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                        %mn 2
                      %mo :
                      %mi F
                      %mi B
                      %mo →
                      %mi Z
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde g_2: F B \to Z
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi B
                      %msub
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                        %mi A
                      %mi U
                      %mi Y
                      %msubsup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mn ∞
                        %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (B \coprod_A U Y)_\infty^f
            %p
              To show that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi B
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                      %mi A
                    %mi U
                    %mi Y
                    %msubsup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mn ∞
                      %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y \to (B \coprod_A U Y)_\infty^f
              is an acyclic cofibration of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i : A \to B
              is, recall that this morphism is the composite
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi f
                    %mi B
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                      %mi A
                    %mi U
                    %mi Y
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi B
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                      %mi A
                    %mi U
                    %mi Y
                    %msubsup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mn ∞
                      %mi f
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Y \stackrel{f}{\to} B \coprod_A U Y \to (B \coprod_A U Y)_\infty^f
                    \\,.
            %p
              Here the first morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              is an acyclic cofibration because it is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushout"} pushout
              of the acyclic cofibration
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monomorphism"} monomorphism
              and by the
              %a{:href => "#SolidityLemma"} remarks in the solidity lemma
              the morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                      %mi A
                    %mi U
                    %mi Y
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi B
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                      %mi A
                    %mi U
                    %mi Y
                    %msubsup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mn ∞
                      %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B \coprod_A U Y \to (B \coprod_A U Y)_\infty^f
              is an acyclic cofibration. Hence so is the composite of the two.
          %h3#transferred_model_structure Transferred model structure
          .un_theorem
            %h6#theorem_3 Theorem
            %p
              Under the above conditions,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Alg
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Alg C
              becomes a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
              with the
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transferred+model+structure"} transferred model structure
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Alg
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Alg C
              are those morphisms that are so in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
          %p
            This appears as (
            %a{:href => "#Nikolaus"}> Nikolaus, def. 2.15
            ).
          .proof
            %h6#proof_7 Proof
            %p
              This follows from the
              %a{:href => "#Solidity"} above result
              that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              is a
              %em solid functor
              as described in detail at
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/solid+functor"} solid functor
              by observing that the
              %em acyclicity condition
              required there follows as in the discussion of the solidity of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "#SolidityLemma"} above
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              are
              = succeed "s." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monomorphism"} monomorphism
            %p
              We spell out the argument, following (
              %a{:href => "#Nikolaus"}> Nikolaus
              ).
            %p
              By the conditions listed at
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transferred+model+structure"} transferred model structure
              it is sufficient to check that
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi U
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
                  preserves
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+object"} small object
                  = succeed "s;" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filtered+colimit"} filtered colimit
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi U
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
                  sends
                  = succeed "s" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sequential+colimit"} sequential colimit
                  = succeed "s" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushout"} pushout
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi F
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
                  of generating acyclic cofibrations to weak equivalences.
            %p
              The first item is true by the
              %a{:href => "#LimitsAndColimits"} above discussion
              of filtered colimits in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Alg
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Alg C
            %p
              That the second item holds follows from the above
              %a{:href => "#PushoutLemma"} pushout lemma
              which asserts that
              = succeed "-images" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              = succeed "-images" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              preserves filtered colimits, which implies that it preserves the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transfinite+composition"} transfinite composition
              of these acyclic cofibrations.
          .un_corllary
            %h6#corollary_2 Corollary
            %p
              The functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              preserves acyclic cofibrations.
          .un_theorem
            %h6#theorem_4 Theorem
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+adjunction"} Quillen adjunction
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi F
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mi Alg
                    %mi C
                    %mover
                      %munder
                        %mo →
                        %mi U
                      %mover
                        %mo ←
                        %mi F
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (F \dashv U) : Alg C \stackrel{\overset{F}{\leftarrow}}{\underset{U}{\to}}
                    C
            %p
              is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalence"} Quillen equivalence
          %p
            This appears as (
            %a{:href => "#Nikolaus"}> Nikolaus, theorem 2.18
            )
          .proof
            %h6#proof_8 Proof
            %p
              We observe that the unit and counit of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi F
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (F \dashv U)
              are both weak equivalences:
            %p
              the unit of the adjunction is
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to X_\infty
              is by the
              %a{:href => "#DefOfXInfty"} above construction
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transfinite+composition"} transfinite composition
              of acyclic cofibrations (in fact a fibrant replacement) hence in particular a weak equivalence. Moreover, the unit is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/section"} section
              of the counit in that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi F
                            %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mi Id
                            %mo ↘
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    X &amp;\to&amp; F X
                    \\\
                    \&amp; {}_{\mathllap{Id}}\searrow &amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    \&amp;&amp; X
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              Hence by
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+with+weak+equivalences"} 2-out-of-3
              also
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi F
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to F X
              is a weak equivalence.
            %p
              This implies that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi F
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (F \dashv U)
              induces an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalence of categories
              on the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+categories"} homotopy categories
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              equals its total right
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+functor"} derived functor
              (since every object in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Alg
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Alg C
              is fibrant) this means that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi F
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (F \dashv)
              is a Quillen equivalence.
          %h3#LocalPresentability Local presentability and combinatoriality
          .un_prop
            %h6#proposition_4 Proposition
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+presentable+category"} locally presentable category
              then so is
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Alg
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Alg C
          .proof
            %h6#proof_9 Proof
            %p
              By the
              %a{:href => "#Monadicity"} above
              we know that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Alg
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Alg C
              is the category of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebras+over+a+monad"} algebras over a monad
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi F
                      %mo :
                      %mi C
                      %mo →
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U\circ F : C \to C
            %p
              We invoke the
              %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/locally%20presentable%20category#AlgebrasOverAnAccessibleMonad"} theorem on local presentability of categories of algebras
              discussed at
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+presentable+category"} locally presentable category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \circ F
              is an
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/accessible+functor"} accessible functor
              = succeed "s." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filtered+colimit"} filtered colimit
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              is a left adjoint and hence preserves all colimits, while we checked
              %a{:href => "#LimitsAndColimits"} above
              that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              preserves filtered colimits.
          .un_corollary
            %h6#corollary_3 Corollary
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/combinatorial+model+category"} combinatorial model category
              then so is
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Alg
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Alg C
          %h2#examples Examples
          %h3#AlgebaicHigherCategories
            Algebraic
            = succeed "-groupoids" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
          %p
            The standard
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+sets"} model structure on simplicial sets
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi sSet
                    %mi Quillen
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sSet_{Quillen}
            models the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9EGrpd"} ∞Grpd
            of
            = succeed "s:" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} ∞-groupoid
            = succeed "es." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+complex"} Kan complex
            = succeed "-groupoid" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/k-morphism"} k-morphism
            %em chosen
            \.
          %p
            An algebraic fibrant object in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi sSet
                    %mi Quillen
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sSet_{Quillen}
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+complex"} Kan complex
            with a chosen filler for each
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/horn"} horn
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+Kan+complex"} algebraic Kan complex
            (see
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+T-complex"} simplicial T-complex
            for a related but much stricter notion). This means precisely that all possible composites and all possible inverses are chosen. So the Quillen equivalence
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi sSet
                    %mi Quillen
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mo ←
                  %mi Alg
                  %msub
                    %mi sSet
                    %mi Quillen
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  sSet_{Quillen} \stackrel{\leftarrow}{\to} Alg sSet_{Quillen}
          %p
            induces an equivalence from an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+definition+of+higher+category"} algebraic definition of ∞-groupoids
            to a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+definition+of+higher+categories"} geometric definition
          %h3#algebraic_categories
            Algebraic
            = succeed "-categories" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
          %p
            Similarly, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+for+quasi-categories"} model structure for quasi-categories
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi sSet
                    %mi Joyal
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sSet_{Joyal}
            models
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-categories"} (∞,1)-categories
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-categories"} quasi-categories
            = succeed "." do
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+quasi-category"} algebraic quasi-category
            = succeed "-categories" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
          %p
            But equipping a quasi-category with the structure of an algebraic fibrant object precisely means choosing such composites. Accordingly, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalence"} Quillen equivalence
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi sSet
                    %mi Joyal
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mo ←
                  %mi Alg
                  %msub
                    %mi sSet
                    %mi Joyal
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  sSet_{Joyal} \stackrel{\leftarrow}{\to} Alg sSet_{Joyal}
          %p
            establishes an equivalence of an algebraic with the standard geometric model for
            = succeed "-categories." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+model+category"} algebraic model category
          %h2#references References
          %p The model structure on algebraic fibrant objects was introduced and discussed in
          %ul#Nikolaus
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thomas+Nikolaus"}> Thomas Nikolaus
              ,
              %em Algebraic models for higher categories
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1003.1342"}> arXiv
              )
          %p A survey is in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thomas+Nikolaus"} Thomas Nikolaus
              Talk on
              %em Algebraic models for higher categories
              (
              %a{:href => "http://www.math.uni-hamburg.de/home/nikolaus/AlgMod.pdf"}> here
              )
          %p
            The refined
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+object+argument"} small object argument
            that is being used in the construction of the left adjoint
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo :
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mi Alg
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F : C \to Alg C
            is along the lines of the discussion in
          %ul#Garner
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Richard+Garner"}> Richard Garner
              ,
              %em Understanding the small object argument
              Applied Categorical Structures, 17(3):247–285, 2009 (
              %a{:href => "http://www.dpmms.cam.ac.uk/~rhgg2/CT07/CT07.pdf"}> pdf
              )
        .revisedby
          %p
